  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is weakened because it only covers serious events and excludes minor overheating/smoke reporting. S2 sets a 5% permanent cap with a 36-month transition for existing models but lacks a numeric interim cap, and gives per-model results to purchasers/regulators but not the general public. S3 and S4 satisfy both companies' red lines with a 6-year retrofit deadline and 36-month suppression deadline, while S5 imposes a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger with prompt notice and no transition, which is strict for Halcyon."
